            "spellcastingPreparation": "spontaneous",
            "terms": [
                [
                    "The Declaration",
                    "<strong>The rule the whole class hangs on.</strong> Before any Paradise-Touched effect resolves, you privately choose <em>Signal</em> or <em>Static</em> (§3). You do not announce it. The table does not get told."
                ],
                [
                    "Signal",
                    "<strong>Channel open wide.</strong> The effect gets better — usually +2 status to the roll, or one step up the ladder. If it fails, you take force damage and gain a point of Signal Drift."
                ],
                [
                    "Static",
                    "<strong>Channel kept narrow.</strong> No benefit. Failing costs you nothing at all. But a <em>success</em> is subject to a secret DC 5 flat check, and on a failed flat check the result is false and the GM tells it to you as though it were true."
                ],
                [
                    "Bandwidth",
                    "<strong>Your class resource.</strong> Pays for Glimpses — the Aperture abilities in §2. Regained by <em>Re-sync</em>. Separate from your spell slots, which work like any spontaneous occult caster's."
                ],
                [
                    "Re-sync",
                    "<strong>Your Refocus.</strong> Ten minutes doing nothing but listening. Recovers 1 Bandwidth. Doing it in a settlement makes people nervous, and they are right to be."
                ],
                [
                    "Glimpse",
                    "<strong>An Aperture ability bought with Bandwidth</strong> — one at 1st, 7th, and 15th, set by which Aperture you chose. Declared Signal or Static like everything else."
                ],
                [
                    "Signal Drift",
                    "<strong>The permanent one.</strong> A 0–10 track that only ever goes up, and only when a Signal-declared effect fails (§4). Deliberately built as the sibling of the cybernetic Drift track — same bands, same one-way door, different axis."
                ],
                [
                    "Aperture",
                    "<strong>Your subclass</strong> — The Archive, The Chorus, or The Render (§2). Chosen at 1st level. It decides which part of Paradise is open to you, and therefore what it hands you when you ask."
                ],
                [
                    "The Feed",
                    "<strong>The signal itself.</strong> The ambient broadcast every live Paradise node puts out, whether or not anyone's tuned in. What you draw on when you Re-sync, and what a body thinned far enough by Drift has to substitute for sleep."
                ]
            ],
